 "annualKpisNote": "Company-reported. receivables = gross credit-card receivables at March (₹ cr); spends = total card spends (₹ cr; FY23-FY24 from the ₹'000 cr chart, so rounded); cifMm = cards in force (million); newAccountsLakh = new accounts (lakh). Company ratios (yield, NIM, cost of funds, gross credit cost, ROA, ROE, cost-to-income) are on monthly averages from FY24 (quarterly before) and differ from our year-end-average ratios: company yield uses interest from cardholders only; company cost-to-income includes other income (recoveries) in the denominator. creditCost = gross credit cost % of average receivables. FY19-FY20 new accounts and CIF in AR FY21 are in '000 (2,840k / 3,408k / 2,685k) and converted to lakh. AR FY26 MD letter says Mar-26 gross receivables ₹56,962 cr; every other page says ₹56,926 cr (used).",
